## Goal
Magic-link emails currently show **Supabase Auth** as sender and a “powered by Supabase” footer. Travellers won’t recognise that — change to **Trip Ready**.

## How (when they have time)
1. Supabase → **Authentication → Email Templates → Magic Link** — Trip Ready subject/body (keep `{{ .ConfirmationURL }}`).
2. Supabase → **Authentication → SMTP** — custom SMTP (Resend/SendGrid/etc.) with **Sender name:** `Trip Ready` and a verified from-address. Required to change the inbox From name and drop default branding; also raises email rate limits.

## Why this matters soon
Custom SMTP also fixes the painful **email rate limit** (built-in mailer allows only a few magic links per hour — easy to hit while testing).

Do not implement custom SMTP in code until the user asks to return to this.
